{"title":"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A line segment is divided so that the lesser part is to the greater part as the greater part is to the whole. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the ratio of the lesser part to the greater part, then the value of \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14b68e90ffe7da6035b6e43f97b5b1b7a024d1b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R^{[R^{(R^2+R^{-1})}+R^{-1}]}+R^{-1}\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/2/b22a232b6b309542ea1f24aafa5f2a01833b426b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 2 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }2R \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } R^{-1} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 2+R^{-1} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }2+R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"469\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the length of the shorter segment and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the length of the longer segment. We're given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/e/24e5f115e09de2aea5b45703a2379ee127a8a5e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{l}=\\frac{l}{w+l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"85\" height=\"39\" />. Cross-multiplying, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92ca2f24f7468632fcecefba3ecce46fac8c36d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^2+wl=l^2\\implies w^2+wl-l^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"280\" height=\"16\" />. Now we divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99a7769d50c24df6fd19aa599c2bcbb82d4e3414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2$\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/790c3d8e66d75a21b9f565d87bed00c212bfde27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{w}{l}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{w}{l}\\right)-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"171\" height=\"36\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd5410c5764aae9a653da524e333dffc44ffa354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2+R-1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>From this, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/7371a68d1af8b8f1ee576a08b3edfcd32d681660.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2=-R+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />. Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792feac8dd37d22307217056e46c8a22d1f5c380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=-1+\\frac{1}{R}\\implies R^{-1}=R+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"251\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312726a93fa2b0bb29dd3817ba3c93d3e0d4b3f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2+R^{-1}=-R+1+R+1=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"259\" height=\"16\" />. Finally, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/f/81f81910cbdcdf10b2422167510c6c873f58381a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R^{[R^{(R^2+R^{-1})}+R^{-1}]}+R^{-1}=R^{[R^2+R^{-1}]}+R^{-1}=R^2+R^{-1}= \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}2}.\\]\" width=\"484\" height=\"31\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME\" title=\"1974 AHSME\">1974 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1974 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1974 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1974\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1974 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1974_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\